; Managed by WhaCP (installer/install.sh).
;
; WhaCP's greylisting and mail limits are Postfix policy services started
; by systemd socket units (whacp-greylist.socket, whacp-mailrate.socket).
; Their sockets live in Postfix's private folder, where smtpd reaches them:
; /var/spool/postfix/private (postfix_private_t). The distribution policy
; does not let systemd (init_t) create a socket there ("avc: denied
; { add_name } ... comm=systemd ... tclass=dir"), so the socket units
; failed on SELinux-enforcing systems. This allows exactly that, nothing
; else: the sockets take the folder's type, as Postfix's own do.
(allow init_t postfix_private_t (dir (search getattr write add_name remove_name)))
(allow init_t postfix_private_t (sock_file (create unlink getattr setattr)))
